  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{試|し} (try, test) + {着|ちゃく} (wearing)\n\nSHOPPING VOCABULARY:\n・{試着室|しちゃくしつ} - fitting room, changing room\n・{試着|しちゃく}できますか - May I try this on?\n\nRELATED:\n・{試飲|しいん} - drink tasting\n・{試食|ししょく} - food tasting\n・{着替|きが}える - to change clothes\n\nUSAGE:\nAsking 「{試着|しちゃく}してもいいですか」 is the standard polite way to request to try on clothes in Japanese stores.",
